      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should clarify, this is coming from the Oculus side where we\u0027re running Android 14 on our headsets. The corrupted oat files we\u0027re seeing are coming from many different unrelated apps (both 1st and 3rd party). We observed their hash changing vs when they were first installed so dex2oat was a suspect.\n\nI also didn\u0027t find any direct mechanism by which this was being called and the FD path looks safe to me. We\u0027re rolling this out as a precautionary step mostly to rule out dex2oat as the issue.\n\nIf you think the change is unnecessary for mainline AOSP that\u0027s definitely fair.",
